      'idiom':               { k2: 'A saying with a hidden meaning: "hit a wall".', g35: 'A phrase that means something different from its words, like "throw in the towel".', g68: 'A phrase whose meaning is different from the meaning of its separate words.' },
      'word parts':          { k2: 'Parts of a word, like re- in reread.', g35: 'The pieces of a word: prefix, root and suffix.', g68: 'The prefix, root and suffix of a word, which can help you work out its meaning.' },
      'fix-up strategy':     { k2: 'What you do when lost: read it again.', g35: 'What to do when you are lost: reread, slow down, ask.', g68: 'A move you make when understanding breaks down: reread, slow down, read on, ask or look it up.' },
